des.java` null-guard — finding is incorrect, leaving it in\n\nI disagree with the conclusion that this is an unrelated change to split out, for two concrete reasons:\n\n**1. It is load-bearing for the acceptance behaviour the spec is about.** The spec says **400** rejections must be `application/problem+json`. The acceptance test's 400 case is an owner posted with `city` omitted. `city` is a required field, so bean validation *should* reject it with a 400 `ProblemDetail` — but `PostcodeValidator` runs in the same validation pass and calls `Postcodes.isValidForCity(postcode, null)`, where `CITY_REGIONS.get(null)` on a `Map.of` map throws an NPE. Bean Validation wraps that as a `ValidationException`, which surfaces as a **500**. Without the guard, the test asserts 400 and gets 500 — I verified this is exactly the failure (`Status expected:<400> but was:<500>`) before adding the guard. So this is not a tangential correctness fix; it is precisely what makes a **400 rejection** reach the problem+json path the spec requires. Removing it breaks the mandated acceptance behaviour.\n\n**2. The \"split into its own commit\" remedy can't apply here** — this working directory is not a git repository, so there are no separate commits to split into. The change is a single in-tree edit.\n\nI'll also note the guard isn't really foreign to `Postcodes`: its own javadoc states \"a city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode,\" and a `null` city trivially has no known region — so `city == null ? null : CITY_REGIONS.get(city)` is just making the utility honour its documented contract null-safely, consistent with the sibling null-postcode guard right above it.\n\nI considered relocating the guard into `PostcodeValidator` to sit nearer the \"validation\" layer, but that would leave `Postcodes.isValidForCity` itself NPE-prone for any future caller, so keeping the fix in the utility is the more robust placement.\n\nNet: RFC7807 structure unchanged (reviewer approved it); the `Postcodes` guard stays because it is required for the 400 rejection to render as problem+json. Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).","ttft_ms":42842,"type":"result","duration_ms":77502,"uuid":"16702259-716d-42db-96d9-46bc49b1c6c6","ttft_stream_ms":1661,"time_to_request_ms":623,"first_content_frame_ms":1661,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
